Subject: normalise and dedupe bytes dht_prefix from the DHT model index

fetch_health_state assigns dht_prefix straight from the _petals.models DHT
index onto ModelInfo *after* ModelInfo.from_dict(), so pydantic never coerces
it -- pydantic dataclasses do not validate on attribute assignment. hivemind
returns record subkeys as bytes when they are not stored as UTF-8-decodable
strings, so the index holds a mix of str and bytes prefixes.

That causes two distinct failures:

1. Sorting the mixed list raises
   TypeError: '<' not supported between instances of 'bytes' and 'str'

2. The same prefix can appear under BOTH its bytes and str form. Once decoded
   they collide, duplicating the model and its block_uids. get_remote_module_infos
   then blocks forever on a query built from duplicated uids -- the updater
   thread parks in concurrent.futures result() with no timeout, so the service
   hangs silently with no traceback.

Decode bytes at the point of assignment, dedupe by the normalised prefix, and
make the sort key total via str() so one malformed record cannot take down the
updater.

The decode also matters beyond the sort: dht_prefix is interpolated into
block_uids, where a bytes value renders as b'Foo' and silently fails to match
server-announced UIDs -- showing the model as "broken" rather than crashing.

Upstream: https://github.com/petals-infra/health.petals.dev
Developed-against: 30d00fb644a0b1333e37278d43735b29623f9932
Note: the Dockerfile clones upstream unpinned, so this patch tracks a moving
target. `git apply` runs without fuzz, so if upstream changes these lines the
build fails loudly rather than silently dropping the fix -- refresh the patch
against the new revision at that point.
---
--- a/health.py
+++ b/health.py
@@ -41,10 +41,18 @@
                 model_info = ModelInfo.from_dict(model.value)
                 if model_info.repository is None or not model_info.repository.startswith("https://huggingface.co/"):
                     continue
+                if isinstance(dht_prefix, bytes):
+                    dht_prefix = dht_prefix.decode("utf-8", errors="replace")
                 model_info.dht_prefix = dht_prefix
                 model_info.official = False
                 custom_models.append(model_info)
-        models.extend(sorted(custom_models, key=lambda info: (-info.num_blocks, info.dht_prefix)))
+        # The DHT index can hold the same prefix under both its bytes and str
+        # form. After decoding they collide, which would duplicate the model and
+        # its block_uids -- and a query built from duplicated uids hangs.
+        deduped = {}
+        for info in custom_models:
+            deduped.setdefault(info.dht_prefix, info)
+        models.extend(sorted(deduped.values(), key=lambda info: (-info.num_blocks, str(info.dht_prefix))))
     logger.info(f"Fetching info for models {[info.name for info in models]}")
 
     block_uids = [f"{model.dht_prefix}{UID_DELIMITER}{i}" for model in models for i in range(model.num_blocks)]
